<title>UK: UK's Discovery Inns Plc pulls float plans.</title>
<headline>UK's Discovery Inns Plc pulls float plans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Discovery Inns Plc said in a statement on Monday that it had decided not to proceed with its planned flotation due to unfavourable market conditions.</p>
<p>The company had originally planned a full market listing sometime in December. The company was expected to have come to market with a value of between 40.0 and 50.0 million stg.</p>
<p>The sponsor to the float was Hambros Bank.</p>
<p>- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
